The only script whose logic and output match the sanity–checks done on the raw data is 1result.sql.  
It correctly  
• identifies the globally most‑active assignee in A61,  
• picks that assignee’s busiest year,  
• ranks jurisdictions by patent count in that year, and  
• returns the top five codes in the expected order (“US,AU,EG,CA,NZ”).  

The other two queries either mis‑rank the jurisdictions (0result.sql) or even miss the dominant US jurisdiction altogether (2result.sql), showing that their counting logic is flawed.

